{"id":"chino","lemma":"chino","pos":"noun","rank":1796,"glosses":["gobbledygook (an incomprehensible language)","a Chinese restaurant","(US) variety store, dollar store, dime store, five-and-dime, (UK) pound shop (owned by a Chinese immigrant)"],"ipa":"/ˈt͡ʃino/","gender":"m","forms":{"plural":"chinos"},"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-Millars-chino.wav","formAudio":{"chinos":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-Eavqwiki-chinos.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"Me suena a chino.","en":"It's Greek to me.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/453219"},{"text":"¿Cuántos amigos chinos tienes?","en":"How many Chinese friends do you have?","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/525368"},{"text":"Él habla chino fluido.","en":"He is fluent in Chinese.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/461685"},{"text":"¿Puedes comer con palillos chinos?","en":"Do you know how to eat with chopsticks?","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/78096"},{"text":"Él también estudia chino.","en":"He studies Chinese as well.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/639273"}]}